    "date"     : "March 27, 2021",
    "excerpt"  : "This article will discuss the basic knowledge needed in order for one to integrate CSS into bits of an HTML page. Examples include having an image fade in or having text slide onto the screen from right-to-left.\n\n\n\nLet’s start with the basics: Whe...",
  "content"  : "This article will discuss the basic knowledge needed in order for one to integrate CSS into bits of an HTML page. Examples include having an image fade in or having text slide onto the screen from right-to-left.\n\n\n\nLet’s start with the basics: Where exactly in your HTML file should your CSS reside?\n\nAn HTML file uses the tag below to store the information on how HTML\n elements should render on your website. Within this style tag is where the values (color, size, font, etc.) you want\n  to change should be declared.\n\n &amp;lt;style&amp;gt; here is where you would add any CSS code &amp;lt;/style&amp;gt; \n\n\n So now that we’ve covered where the CSS resides, how is it formatted and implemented? \n\nFor more straight-forward things like transforming text and margin height you use the name of the item (p, h1, h2\n, etc.) that you want to modify and in curly brackets put all of the different ‘transformations’. An example is shown\n below:\n\n  h1{\n   text-align: center;\n   text-transform: uppercase;\n   color: #4CAF50;\n    margin-top: 0px;\n    margin-bottom: 0px;\n }\n \n\nOk, now that we’ve covered the basics let’s delve into some more complicated CSS!  How do animations work in CSS\n? \n\nLet’s look at the code for moving text from the right side of the window to the left side. Credits to this website\n.\n\ndiv.slide-left {\n  width:100%;\n  overflow:hidden;\n}\ndiv.slide-left p {\n  animation: slide-left 12s;\n}\n\n@keyframes slide-left {\n  from {\n    margin-left: 100%;\n    width: 100%;\n  }\n\n  to {\n    margin-left: 0%;\n    width: 100%;\n  }\n}\n\ncoding tid-bit - @keyframes specify the animation code by declaring the style change at the start to the end\n (depicted by the ‘from’ and ‘to’)\n"
} ,
  
